WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.810
- [Mark] All right, Edgar.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.643
- Yes, sir.

00:00:04.643 --> 00:00:05.510
- [Mark] Where did you grow up?

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.020
Where are you from originally?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.350
- [Edgar] Originally Franklin, Virginia.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.860
I've been out here since, I came out here

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.160
when I was five years old.

00:00:13.615 --> 00:00:15.000
- [Mark] And, you grew
up in which neighborhood?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.250
- I grew up here in
Watts, Nickerson Gardens.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.183
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:19.183 --> 00:00:20.620
You had both parents as a kid or not?

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.420
- No, just my mother.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.803
My dad is,

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:28.050
he was still in Franklin, Virginia.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.680
Me, my mom, and my sister came out here

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.893
and I was just, just me and my sister.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.880
- [Mark] And how would you
describe your childhood?

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.920
- Excuse me?
- How was your childhood?

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.143
- My childhood?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.610
Well, the best way I can put it is,

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:49.373
I grew up in a violent neighborhood.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.800
They had just about anything you wanted,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.700
as far as drugs, liquor, whatever,

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.920
my surrounding was gang banging.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.793
And you know, down here, life.

00:01:06.671 --> 00:01:08.860
- [Mark] And you stayed at home

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.900
with your mom until how long?

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.600
- I stayed home with my mom
til I was about 12 years old.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.910
I ran away from home.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:21.560
I came downtown LA.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.560
And I stayed downtown LA for
about three and a half years.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.383
I went back home,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.600
and got into a little trouble

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.110
but went to jail, juvenile hall.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:41.870
Juvenile hall to a County jail,

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.969
from the County jail to prison.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:45.802
- [Mark] Did you go to high school?

00:01:45.802 --> 00:01:47.370
- Excuse me?
- Did you go to high school?

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.320
- I went to high school for three days.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:54.883
And the reason why, the
neighborhood I stayed in,

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.120
was a gang,

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.010
whenever the gang was bounty hunters

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.580
from the Nickerson Gardens.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:03.638
The school I went to was Jordan High,

00:02:03.638 --> 00:02:07.310
and they had a project

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.510
called the Jordan Downs.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.890
The Jordan Downs was cribbed,

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.620
and we was bloods.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.850
And by me being a blood,
they kind of knew my face

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.609
and was like, hey, why shouldn't I,

00:02:19.609 --> 00:02:20.612
I shouldn't Faisal,

00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:22.778
my nickname was Faisal.

00:02:22.778 --> 00:02:25.000
And they're like, ain't your name Faisal?

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.060
I'm like, yo.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.230
They said, don't you sit
in Nickerson Gardens?

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.360
And before I can answer the question,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.350
it was like almost the whole
school was coming towards me

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:39.030
which I knew was bad, so
I ran and I, like I said,

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.750
it was only for like three days.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.320
I said, I can't go,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.231
because I was in the wrong neighborhood.

00:02:44.231 --> 00:02:46.131
The school was the wrong neighborhood.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.171
And from there

00:02:49.171 --> 00:02:53.470
I've been homeless still.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.260
- [Mark] And drugs or
alcohol came in the picture

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.096
for you when?

00:02:56.096 --> 00:02:58.210
- Alcohol, I was about

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.990
nine years old,

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.460
when I started drinking,

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:07.930
and what started me
drinking was my uncles,

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:12.030
my aunties used to always
come over to my mom house

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:17.010
and they used to play
cards, gamble, and drink.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.432
My uncle, my favorite
uncle, he drunk one five

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.710
(yawns) excuse me.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.980
He got Bacardi, Bacardi was like

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.900
one, five, one.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.450
And usually people would
drink it back with Coke.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:35.273
My uncle, he would drink it by itself.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.534
He was my favorite uncle.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:43.534
And one day he came over,
picked me up, took me with him.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.310
And that's when I started drinking

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.143
with my uncle.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.310
- [Mark] And at home with your mom,

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.580
she was into drugs or alcohol?

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.413
- Yes.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.837
She was into drugs and alcohol.

00:03:54.837 --> 00:03:59.837
And it would be times where she did have

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.600
what she wanted

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.613
and she would take it
out on me and my sister.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:11.180
And I felt like she didn't care about me.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.120
Why should I stay here?

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.460
And I ran away from home,
but drugs had a lot to do

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.560
with me running away too,
because I was like my mom

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.400
to a certain extent, you know,
and I can get what I want.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:30.240
I would steal stuff, man, take
this stuff that didn't belong

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.230
to me and bring a problem to my house.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:38.510
And the best way I knew how to get it

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.700
was to run away.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.981
And they started me going to jail.

00:04:42.981 --> 00:04:45.590
- [Mark] And what kind of
stuff were you getting into

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.950
at that point?

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:50.670
- Well, gang banging, females,

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.390
anything I could get into basically.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.690
- [Mark] The prison time
you did was for what?

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.800
- Taking stuff from
somebody, stolen property,

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.273
breaking into houses, breaking into cars,

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.823
jacking people,

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.943
you know, all kinds of stupid stuff.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.880
Now at that time it wasn't stupid,

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.140
because I was under an influence

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.270
and my mind

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.163
was basically,

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.820
I guess on one thing
and it was getting drugs

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.250
and I didn't have a job.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.050
So it was only one way
I knew how to get it.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.080
And that was, you know,
get somebody back there

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.510
and take from them.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.990
- [Mark] Yeah, and that was crack cocaine

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:36.823
that you were chasing?

00:05:36.823 --> 00:05:38.400
- That was, yes.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.233
Yes.

00:05:40.493 --> 00:05:41.830
- [Mark] And do you have kids of your own?

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.040
- No, I have no kids.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:48.493
What really started me with
crack cocaine was my mom.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.359
She was smoking.

00:05:51.359 --> 00:05:56.359
(yawns) And I wanted to
see what it was like.

00:05:57.458 --> 00:06:00.800
And I went and got some,

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.540
my mom had to choose,

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.370
so I brought it back to
her and she like looked

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:10.330
at me kind of crazy,
but she wanted some too.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:14.400
So I started smoking with my
mom's and I was getting high

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.400
with my mom's for a long
time, until she passed away.

00:06:21.549 --> 00:06:23.530
- [Mark] And how much prison
time have you done in all?

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.240
- The most prison time I've
done, was two and a half years.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.010
- [Mark] But in total?

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:29.510
- Total, two and a half years.

00:06:30.902 --> 00:06:33.160
- [Mark] Oh, so not that much prison time?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:38.080
- No, it was basically in and
out because I was on parole.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:38.950
Okay?

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.040
But me being on parole, when I got out,

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.603
it was certain things that I had to do.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:47.493
I was still getting high,

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.011
so I didn't report

00:06:50.011 --> 00:06:54.140
(yawns) because when I be put,

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.590
they would test me,

00:06:55.590 --> 00:07:00.240
they would give me a drug
test and I know I'm dirty.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.860
So it's like, I'm turning myself in, okay?

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:07.430
I felt like this at that time,

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:10.650
if I gotta be for it or turn myself in,

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.400
I'm not going to do it, okay?

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.520
Your job is either catch me

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.360
or I turn myself in and I
wasn't gonna turn myself in.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:24.010
So anytime I got stuck, but
not in (indistinct), you know,

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.540
they would take me in.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.340
That's the only way they would take me in,

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.300
and I got to be a violation of parole,

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.990
because I didn't report.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.130
So they would take me back.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:36.030
I had to go back to prison
for a certain amount of time.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.493
Eight months, six months, you know.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.317
- [Mark] And you've been
living on the street

00:07:40.317 --> 00:07:41.740
for how long now?

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:42.630
(sighs)

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.780
- I'm 56.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.780
I've been on the streets since I was 12.

00:07:47.957 --> 00:07:50.260
- [Mark] And today you
are living in a tent?

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.820
- Yes.
- Down here on Skid Row?

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:52.940
- Yes.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.756
Right down the street.

00:07:54.756 --> 00:07:56.880
- [Mark] And what do you do for money now?

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.200
- I wash cars.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.000
I wash windows.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.910
I sweep, I do cleanup.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.150
You know.
- You're still using crack?

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:06.983
- Yes.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.223
- [Mark] Have you ever been clean?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.830
- Only time I was clean
was when I got locked up.

00:08:14.343 --> 00:08:17.151
- [Mark] Then you get out and
you eventually just go back?

00:08:17.151 --> 00:08:19.751
- When I get out, my first
stop is the liquor store.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.577
'Cause I mean, I really, really

00:08:27.463 --> 00:08:28.700
like the drinking.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:32.269
I like that feeling that
it gave me, you know,

00:08:32.269 --> 00:08:36.805
and I just, it was something that I enjoy.

00:08:36.805 --> 00:08:38.830
- [Mark] When you were
a child, did you have,

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.350
what kind of dreams did
you have for your life?

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.680
Did you, do you have any thing that you-

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:46.740
- I wanted to be, I wanted
to write, write books.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:48.060
I like to write poem.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.190
That's what I did, I started writing poems

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.240
when I was locked up.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:53.730
Now I (indistinct).

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.300
Write the things that come to
my mind, things on my mind,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.880
things I see in people,
other people, you know,

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.303
I like to move around like that.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:10.018
- [Mark] Have you ever been in love?

00:09:10.018 --> 00:09:10.851
- In love?

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:14.680
Yes, almost every female I've been,

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:18.120
really have been in
love (laughs), you know,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.910
but it was just one particular
girl that I was in love,

00:09:22.823 --> 00:09:25.543
I would do anything for her, anything.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:30.213
If she asked me robbing
a bank, I probably would.

00:09:31.389 --> 00:09:33.710
- [Mark] How do you think
outsiders as they drive

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:38.710
through Skid Row, what their
impression is of people,

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.973
that are living on the street like you do?

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.680
- Ooh, I don't know how to describe that.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:47.570
I see

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.030
people that in their mind

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:57.530
call yourself pretty good,
and they look down on us,

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.250
on the people who lived on the streets.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.853
And I met this one guy.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:06.313
It was on the streets.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.330
And about a week after

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:14.570
I was at the gas station with
a hustler and he drove up

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:18.790
to the gas station in a Mercedes, man,

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:19.850
this guy got a tent.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.300
And he was like, you know what?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.210
He say, only reason I was on the street,

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:28.110
I wanted to see what the
street life was about.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.010
He said, man, I got two cars.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:34.530
I got a wife, I got a family,
I got my own business.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:39.060
And he said, here, the
guy handed me like $500,

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:41.750
to say, this for being my friend,

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.600
not looking down on me and not judging me.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:49.600
And it kinda like, it
blew my mind, you know?

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.433
He said, yeah.

00:10:50.433 --> 00:10:53.400
He says, I just want to see
what the street life was about.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.180
Because a lot of people
look down on you guys,

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.970
and won't give you nothing
and they turn their nose up

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.470
when they will pass us.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.540
And it hurts.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.650
You know, I didn't go to school.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:08.043
I went to school, but I
didn't go to the class.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:09.800
You know?

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:13.610
And it's a big difference.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:14.680
You know?

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:17.960
I don't look at myself no
different than anybody else.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:20.030
I don't judge nobody.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.678
You know,

00:11:21.678 --> 00:11:25.090
it's an old saying, everything look good,

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:28.243
ain't always good, everything bad,

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.074
ain't also bad.

00:11:31.074 --> 00:11:33.330
As bad as it looked, you know.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.520
- [Mark] What do you think attracts people

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.100
to this street life?

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.490
I mean, the lack of
responsibility, you think,

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.500
and you never have to work,

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:42.744
you never have to pay taxes.

00:11:42.744 --> 00:11:44.172
You never have to do anything.

00:11:44.172 --> 00:11:47.830
- Well, but street to me,

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.793
street life is people,

00:11:53.017 --> 00:11:55.140
that's into drugs.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:55.973
Okay?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.620
And just about everybody

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:05.170
that's on the streets is into something.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:06.003
Okay?

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:10.103
Like where I'm living at right now.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.470
I feel safer here.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:15.420
I call this my home.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.400
The reason why I call it my home

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:21.050
because it's my surrounding,

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:26.010
I feel better and safer here
than being around somebody,

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.403
work every day.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:29.943
They don't drink.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:33.570
It's a different feeling.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:35.450
It's a different life.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:39.300
So we call this home
because it's street life.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.223
We do what we wanna do.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.510
It's just different from

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:51.960
a person in Beverly Hills,
Hollywood, you know.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.570
- [Mark] You feel like you belong here?

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.930
- Yes.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:59.770
Because if, even though
I'm doing the same thing,

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.770
if I was standing in
Hollywood or Beverly Hills

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.410
I wouldn't feel right
because don't nobody,

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:12.780
ain't too many people up here
in Hollywood or Beverly Hills,

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:13.680
do a video.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.030
They feel, but they went to
school, graduated, you know,

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:18.973
got jobs.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.590
They're better than us.

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:26.130
And I wouldn't feel like, you know.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:30.080
Here I don't have to hide
anything from anybody.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:33.500
As far as you know what I do, you know.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.200
I have to keep nothing from nobody

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.030
because everybody's doing the same thing,

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:42.234
is doing something in that area.

00:13:42.234 --> 00:13:43.067
- [Mark] Do you think you'll be down here

00:13:43.067 --> 00:13:43.998
for the rest of your life?

